---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import tableImage from '../assets/wine-at-table.webp';
import tableSource from '../assets/wine-at-table.source.json';
import { photoCredit } from '../lib/photo-credit';

const credit = photoCredit(tableSource);
---
<Base title="About — Paircraft" description="A pocket guide to a better match between glass and plate.">
  <main class="page-shell max-w-5xl">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)] gap-7 md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,0.9fr)_minmax(0,1.1fr)] md:items-start md:gap-14">
      <div class="relative isolate -mx-5 -mt-8 flex aspect-[4/5] items-end overflow-hidden bg-black px-5 pb-[1.4rem] pt-5 text-on-photo sm:mx-0 sm:mt-0 sm:shadow-[0_4px_4px_rgb(0_0_0/0.25)] md:sticky md:top-36">
        <Image src={tableImage} alt="Two glasses of wine on a table" class="absolute inset-0 -z-20 h-full w-full object-cover" widths={[480, 900]} sizes="(min-width: 768px) 450px, 100vw" loading="eager" />
        <div class="absolute inset-0 -z-10 bg-linear-to-t from-black/80 to-black/15 to-65%" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        {credit && <p class="absolute right-[0.9rem] top-[0.7rem] text-[0.625rem] font-light text-on-photo/70">{credit}</p>}
        <h1 class="font-display text-[2.6rem] font-normal leading-[1.1] md:text-[3.25rem]"><span data-es-value="El vino encuentra su">Wine finds its</span> <em class="not-italic text-hero-accent" data-es-value="mesa">table</em>.</h1>
      </div>
      <div class="min-w-0">
        <p class="font-display text-[1.3rem] italic leading-[1.45]" data-es-value="Una botella, un plato y una buena razón para juntarlos.">A bottle, a plate, and a good reason to put them together.</p>
        <p class="mt-[0.9rem] text-[0.9375rem] font-light leading-[1.65] text-muted" data-es-value="Paircraft es una guía de bolsillo para elegir qué comer con tu vino. Busca una botella, explora sus maridajes y sigue la curiosidad hacia las uvas y regiones que le dan carácter.">Paircraft is a pocket guide to what to eat with your wine. Find a bottle, explore its pairings, and follow your curiosity to the grapes and regions behind it.</p>
        <a class="action mt-[1.3rem]" href="/wines" data-es-value="Encuentra tu botella">Find your bottle</a>
        <section class="mt-10">
          <h2 class="font-display text-[1.6rem] font-normal leading-[1.2]" data-es-value="Tres formas de encontrar el maridaje">Three ways to find the match</h2>
          {/* A swipeable row on phones; a plain stack once the photo sits beside the text. */}
          <dl class="-mx-5 mt-4 grid auto-cols-[78%] grid-flow-col gap-[0.9rem] overflow-x-auto px-5 pb-3 [scrollbar-width:none] snap-x snap-mandatory sm:-mx-8 sm:px-8 md:mx-0 md:auto-cols-auto md:grid-flow-row md:overflow-visible md:px-0 md:pb-0 [&::-webkit-scrollbar]:hidden">
          <div class="snap-start bg-surface px-[1.15rem] pb-[1.35rem] pt-[1.2rem] tile-shadow"><dt class="font-display text-[1.45rem] leading-[1.15]" data-es-value="Armonía">Harmony</dt><dd class="mt-[0.55rem] text-sm font-light leading-[1.6] text-muted" data-es-value="Un plato con cuerpo pide un vino que le siga el paso. Intensidades y texturas encuentran un ritmo común.">A substantial dish wants a wine that can keep up. Weight and texture find a shared rhythm.</dd></div>
          <div class="snap-start bg-surface px-[1.15rem] pb-[1.35rem] pt-[1.2rem] tile-shadow"><dt class="font-display text-[1.45rem] leading-[1.15]" data-es-value="Contraste">Contrast</dt><dd class="mt-[0.55rem] text-sm font-light leading-[1.6] text-muted" data-es-value="La acidez refresca una fritura; el tanino se encuentra con la proteína. La diferencia aporta equilibrio.">Acidity refreshes a fried bite; tannin meets protein. Difference brings balance.</dd></div>
          <div class="snap-start bg-surface px-[1.15rem] pb-[1.35rem] pt-[1.2rem] tile-shadow"><dt class="font-display text-[1.45rem] leading-[1.15]" data-es-value="Realce">Enhancement</dt><dd class="mt-[0.55rem] text-sm font-light leading-[1.6] text-muted" data-es-value="Las notas terrosas de un vino acompañan a los hongos. Un sabor compartido hace que ambos se expresen mejor.">A wine’s earthy notes find a friend in mushrooms. A shared flavour brings out more in both.</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </section>
        <section class="mt-10 max-w-[40rem]">
          <h2 class="font-display text-[1.6rem] font-normal leading-[1.2]" data-es-value="El porqué, en una frase">The why, in one sentence</h2>
          <p class="mt-[0.9rem] text-[0.9375rem] font-light leading-[1.65] text-muted" data-es-value="Cada maridaje tiene un veredicto —decisivo, vale la pena probar o puente arriesgado— y una explicación breve. El veredicto describe la relación entre plato y vino. La cocción, la salsa y tu gusto también cuentan.">Every pairing has a verdict—decisive, worth trying or risky bridge—and a short explanation. The verdict describes the relationship between plate and wine. Cooking, sauce and your own taste matter too.</p>
          <p class="mt-[0.9rem] text-[0.9375rem] font-light leading-[1.65] text-muted" data-es-value="Hecho por Jorge Rondón, desde su formación en hostelería en CUHELAV y su curiosidad por lo que ocurre en la mesa. La guía sigue creciendo botella a botella.">Made by Jorge Rondón, drawing on his hospitality background at CUHELAV and curiosity about what happens at the table. The guide grows bottle by bottle.</p>
          <a href="/pair" class="type-pill mt-5 h-[2.1rem] px-4 text-[0.8125rem] normal-case" data-es-value="¿Ya elegiste el plato?">Already chosen the dish?</a>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
